pgrade or downgrade my plan?",answer:"Yes, you can upgrade or downgrade your subscription at any time. When you upgrade, you'll get immediate access to additional features and message allowances. If you downgrade, your new limits will take effect at the start of your next billing cycle."},{question:"Do unused messages roll over to the next month?",answer:"No, unused messages do not roll over to the next month. Your message allowance resets at the beginning of each billing cycle for all plans."},{question:"What payment methods do you accept?",answer:"We accept all major credit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover) as well as Apple Pay for subscription payments. All payments are processed securely through Stripe."}]},{category:"Features",items:[{question:"How do I use @ to reference templates and components?",answer:"You can reference templates, components, and code snippets using the @ symbol in your prompts. This adds up to 100,000 characters of context (~2,000 lines of code) to help AI create precisely what you envision. For example, you can prompt: 'Create a landing page using @hero-section-template and @pricing-cards'. You can also Shift-click to select and reference multiple components at once."},{question:"Can I create multi-page websites with Aura?",answer:"Yes! Aura supports creating complete multi-page websites. You can create as many pages as you need, link elements to pages for navigation, add smooth page transitions (fade, slide, scale, blur, push, wipe), and publish to friendly subdomains. Each page can share common components and maintain consistent fonts, colors, and styles across your entire site."},{question:"Can I export my site designs out of Aura?",answer:"Absolutely! Everything in Aura is real code—pure HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript. No proprietary frameworks, no vendor lock-in. You can export your entire site as HTML files and upload to Netlify, Vercel, or any hosting platform. You can also export to Figma with organized layers intact, or continue development in v0, Lovable, Cursor, or any code editor. Aura gives you complete ownership and flexibility over your designs."},{question:"What's different from Lovable?",answer:"Aura is a Tailwind design tool that generates real, exportable code—not proprietary formats. While Lovable focuses on full-stack app development, Aura specializes in creating beautiful, responsive web designs with a visual editor that works like Figma. You get 1,700+ templates, 1,400+ components, multi-page sites with navigation, and the ability to export everything as standard HTML/CSS/JS. Think of Aura as a design tool that outputs real code you can use anywhere, while Lovable is more focused on building complete applications with backend functionality."},{question:"What's different from Framer, Webflow, Figma Sites?",answer:"Aura generates real, exportable code—not proprietary formats locked to a platform. Unlike Framer and Webflow which use their own runtime systems, everything in Aura is standard HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript that works everywhere. Unlike Figma Sites which are limited to Figma's ecosystem, Aura designs can be exported and continued in any code editor. You get the visual design experience of Figma, the publishing capabilities of Webflow, but with complete code ownership. Export full sites as files, publish to friendly subdomains, or send designs back to Figma—all while maintaining the freedom to take your code anywhere."}]}],HUa=({isAnimated:e,faqRef:t})=>{const[n,a]=A.useState(new Set),i=l=>{a(c=>{const f=new Set(c);return f.has(l)?f.delete(l):f.add(l),f})};return r.jsx("section",{ref:t,className:"relative z-10",children:r.jsx("div",{className:"bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 rounded-2xl shadow-xl overflow-hidden sm:p-6 lg:p-8 relative z-10 pt-4 pr-4 pb-4 pl-4",children:r.jsxs("div",{className:"max-w-4xl xl:max-w-6xl mx-auto",children:[r.jsxs("div",{className:"md:mb-16 grid md:gri